wildos-store (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Opening a .deb, .flatpakref or .flatpak file shows its own install
    page: what the file says it is, its version against the installed one
    (Already installed, Newer version installed, Update), what it needs
    and what it would remove, and plainly that nothing has checked it. A
    .deb installs through PackageKit, which fetches what it depends on from
    the Wild OS repositories and asks for the password; a package made for
    another system or another kind of computer says so before anything is
    installed. Flatpak files install for the signed-in user.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:50:00 +0000

